        <dc:title>Fire Destroys</dc:title>
        <dc:creator opf:file-as="Ieperen, Geert van" opf:role="aut">Ieperen, Geert van</dc:creator>
        <dc:contributor opf:file-as="calibre" opf:role="bkp">calibre (3.42.0) [https://calibre-ebook.com]</dc:contributor>
        <dc:date>2017-04-01T00:00:00+00:00</dc:date>
        <dc:description>&lt;p class="description"&gt;Rolf, a professional adventurer enters a parallel medieval world where he meets Bloodfire, an anthromorphic wolf. Even though Rolf thinks Bloodfire is impulsive, annoying and completely retarded, he decides to team up for his quest.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Rolf is one of the many agents of SubGeo, an organization that managed to use the absurdity of quantum mechanics to access parallel universes. His job is to enter such a universe and return to earth with magic amulets with useful properties. He only just started his newest mission, when he meets a half-wolf named Bloodfire. Curiously, anthromorphism is unique for Bloodfire, hinting on his wicked background. Rolf's idea to team up with him would have been genius, if Bloodfire wasn't an endlessly enthousiastic, unmature, and impulse-driven animal. But they teamed up anyway, and Bloodfire never leaves.&lt;/p&gt;</dc:description>
        <dc:publisher>Geert van Ieperen</dc:publisher>
